3256..3327 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
3328..3401 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
3402..3479 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
3480..3541 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `(loop ∷ p) then q` is"
3542..3620 Comment "/// `loop ∷ (p then q)`. At zero `spin(Z)` is a call held as the empty word,"
3621..3692 Comment "/// and the composite over it does not yet compute to `spin(a)` (#440)."
